WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.434
Fall is almost here.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.369
That means cold

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:04.137
and flu season is right behind it.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:04.938
And now,

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:05.305
of course,

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:06.506
COVID 19,

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.074
just like we should get a flu shot

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.142
every year, experts say.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:10.410
We'll likely have to get an updated

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.579
COVID 19 shot every year.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.047
The FDA and CDC have approved

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:14.814
the latest COVID

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:15.815
19 vaccines

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.718
from Moderna and Pfizer BioNTech

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.920
as if that is not enough

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.188
doctors are warning that

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:23.923
another respiratory virus,

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.159
RSV, could also be a problem this fall.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:26.960
Oh, goodness.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.028
Well, joining me now to talk about

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:31.064
who needs which vaccine and when is Dr.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:31.464
Sargent

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.799
Matthew is a primary care

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.968
physician and public health specialist.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.302
The public health

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.370
emergency is over,

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.272
but we know COVID isn't going away.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.140
So how important is it

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:40.540
for people

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.610
to at least get this updated vaccine?

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.344
Well, you know,

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.278
let me just break it down.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:45.512
I know

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.846
people are tired of hearing

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.715
about COVID and booster shots.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:49.416
The good news is

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.751
CDC has recommended broadly

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.286
that everybody six months

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:53.720
and older

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.588
should get this new COVID booster.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.090
And just like we get an updated

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:57.724
cell phone,

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.292
you want to make sure that your vaccine

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:00.460
is updated

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.561
to cover the variants

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.763
that are currently in the environment.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.498
You see, most Americans I'm right.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.500
Were probably vaccinated a year ago.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.302
I've got tons of patients who forgot

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.171
when the last booster shot was.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.839
So you get the waning immunity.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.574
And even though you have infections

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.875
in the community,

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.343
the protection from an infection

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.278
also wanes.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.879
So we are actually in a late

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:22.582
summer, early fall surge as we speak.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.184
So what's your reaction to what

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.652
we're hearing from the Florida

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:26.453
surgeon general

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:27.654
who says not only

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:28.021
I mean, he's

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.023
not saying that people don't need it.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.192
He's saying that people under 65

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.360
and those without a serious health risk

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:35.662
should not

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:39.032
get the updated COVID 19 vaccine.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.533
To be honest, Victor,

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:40.900
there's

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.070
definitely a difference in opinion

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.371
among scientists in terms of

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.407
should this be broadly

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:48.541
administered to patients

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:49.409
six months and older,

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:50.610
or should we just

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.712
protect the most vulnerable, the elderly

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.314
and the young kids

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:54.781
and people

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:55.982
that may have asthma,

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.817
diabetes, hypertension.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.352
And I think ultimately, here's

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:00.253
here's the deal.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:02.088
We did not do a good job with the rollout

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:03.356
the last time with vaccines.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.224
I think this time

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:06.226
CDC should just be very clear

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:08.928
and make it simple for everybody.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:09.963
Even if you are a young

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.898
20 year old athlete or an 80 year

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:12.966
old person,

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.968
the risk of COVID is still there.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.803
And with multiple infections,

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.172
Victor, I worry more about long COVID.

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.509
So let's talk about flu and COVID.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:22.809
Right?

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.577
So in terms of the vaccines,

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:25.812
can you get them at the same time?

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:26.513
Do post it out?

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.281
And also, I wanted to ask you,

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:28.515
you know,

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:30.483
I know a couple of people who got the flu

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.852
and COVID basically at the same time.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.454
So in terms of treatment,

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:34.821
I mean, does

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:35.922
one should one

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.123
take priority over the other

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.258
or can you get treated for

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:39.225
both at the same time?

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.894
Well, you know, to answer your first

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.695
or your last question first. Yeah.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:43.530
Ultimately,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.632
anybody can get COVID vaccine

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.634
and flu shot at the same time.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.202
You can get at the same time.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.403
I would recommend that

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.237
if you have the time,

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.138
you're not traveling.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:53.072
You don't have to protect

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.541
an elderly member in the family.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.575
Maybe space it out,

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:57.443
get the flu shot once a week,

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.646
and then the following week at COVID 19,

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:00.480
very rarely

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.481
can you get side effects

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:02.482
to both vaccines.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.384
So I recommend spacing it out

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.285
in terms of treatment.

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:07.053
It's always a nightmare for primary care

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:07.921
physicians like me.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.689
I dread the winter time

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:10.790
because when patients come in

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.525
with a cold, a cough,

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:13.293
you don't really know.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.295
Is it COVID 19 Is it the flu?

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:17.497
Or could it be RSV?

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:18.498
Are these new?

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.433
Are the tests for COVID?

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.469
Picking up the new variants

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.470
and strains

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.406
because we have an executive producer

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.107
whose homes they took six tests.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.809
Yeah, it's not COVID.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:30.743
We now know it's the flu.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:31.544
But when he said

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.412
he took six tests,

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:33.780
my question was,

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.848
does the test know the new variant?

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:36.216
Yeah.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.450
I mean, you are hitting it

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.952
right on the nail, Victor.

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.320
I actually tweeted the other day

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.988
that a lot of patients

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.990
are being misdiagnosed with bronchitis.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.959
So by the time they get to me,

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:46.893
they've tested twice

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:47.427
and they're like, Dr.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:48.561
Matthew, I don't have COVID,

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:49.829
but I am sick.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:50.230
And that's

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.097
because a lot of these

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.099
rapid tests are not picking up

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:54.701
the old Macron strains

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:55.668
and also depends on

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.503
how deep you go up in the nose.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.472
I hate to call it a brain biopsy,

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:00.640
but that's it is a

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.709
I must say it is a brain emergency.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:05.078
I mean, you are going to be cringing.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:07.146
It is painful for a quick second.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.581
So people are not going up

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.249
that,

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.551
you know, deep into the nasal cavity.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:12.185
So, yes,

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:14.354
there are a lot of false negatives

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.388
with a rapid test.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:18.491
I mean, so RSV, flu and COVID.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.425
Great.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.893
Three things to worry about.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.829
Is there any distinction

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.633
in terms of symptoms at all?

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:28.067
You know, with the Omicron infection

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:28.501
right now,

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.636
it tends to be more like cold

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:30.770
like symptoms.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.170
You know,

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.172
it's definitely become more of

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.173
nasal congestion.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.141
Fatigue, headache.

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:35.675
Well, guess what?

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:37.810
That also could be with the flu.

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.312
One thing to distinguish

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:40.546
that is a sudden onset,

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.115
you're going to feel like a ton of bricks

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:44.117
hit you at one time.

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.718
So body aches and fevers.

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.620
So that will distinguish the flu.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.657
But when it comes to RSV and COVID 19,

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:51.858
it can be tough,

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:53.192
can be tough to make,

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.260
to really distinguish

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.062
between between both of them.

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.063
But I tell patients, listen,

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:58.131
if you really want to know

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.432
if you have COVID,

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:00.400
wait a couple of days

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.901
and get the PCR test.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:02.235
I know

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.470
PCR test is not available to everybody.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.439
But it is way more accurate

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:07.874
than the rapid home tests.

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:08.174
Correct.

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.008
My pronunciation

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:10.443
of this, but phenylephrine

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.313
this decongestant in this

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.881
over-the-counter medicines,

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:15.882
the FDA determined

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:17.817
that they just don't work

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:18.151
right

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.352
after being on the market

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:22.121
as safe and effective for 50 years.

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:24.257
They're in DayQuil and Sudafed

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:26.693
and NyQuil NyQuil.

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:30.163
And so aside from how could that happen?

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:32.398
Looking forward, what do people use now?

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:33.666
What works there?

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.568
So many other over-the-counter options

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.170
like Flonase, right?

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:37.503
Of course,

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:38.838
you don't need a doctor's prescription

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:39.372
for that.

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:40.106
And Sudafed,

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:42.141
which is the stronger version of Fennel

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.743
and has always been available

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:44.310
it's just that it's

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.745
now behind the counter.

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:46.679
You actually have to go up

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:47.780
to the pharmacist

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.715
and show your license

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:50.583
because Sudafed was actually used

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.752
as a street drug to make meth.

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:53.453
So fennel,

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:54.253
electronic actually

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:55.188
isn't a lot of products

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:55.788
like you mentioned.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:58.157
And get this, Victor, last year,

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:01.194
over 200 million products of fennel F1

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:01.994
were sold

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:05.732
ripping $1.74 billion in profit.

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.434
That is how common fennel did

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.670
nothing different and did nothing.

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.939
Wow. My gosh. All right.

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:14.640
So as you good to have you in.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.376
Thanks so much for coming. Thank you.

